part.text:
Fixed. The bug was in `specs_setter::on_zero` (include/fmt/core.h:2239), which unconditionally set the fill character to `'0'` even when an explicit alignment option had already been parsed. Per the standard ("If the 0 character and an align option both appear, the 0 character is ignored"), the `0` flag now does nothing when alignment is present:

```cpp
FMT_CONSTEXPR void on_zero() {
  if (specs_.align != align::none) return;
  specs_.align = align::numeric;
  specs_.fill[0] = Char('0');
}
```

Verified behavior:
- `"{:<06}"` with -42 → `-42   ` (was `-42000`)
- `"{:>06}"` with -42 → `   -42` (was `000-42`)
- `"{:06}"` with -42 → `-00042` (unchanged, zero-padding still works)

The full test suite passes (19/20 runnable tests; the `xchar-test` build failure is pre-existing and reproduces on the unmodified baseline).
